# Humanoid Core Companion

> **She has a body, a schedule, and emotions.**
> Not just a persona line, but a full day of life.
> The plugin provides her body, schedule, emotions, and relationship context; how she speaks is still decided by the large model according to her persona.

---

## What it does

“Humanoid Core Companion” is a humanizing plugin for AstrBot. It gives her a body that changes over time, a full day's schedule, and fluctuating emotions, so the character is more than a fixed persona line.

- She has a **body** that changes over time: energy, drowsiness, sleep debt, hunger, and menstrual cycle. It updates without requiring you to speak first;
- She has a **schedule** for the whole day: it is arranged dynamically and can be interrupted. Interrupted tasks are suspended, and she can resume them on her own later;
- She has **emotions and relationships**: affection, mood, and days known, which change gradually with interaction rather than starting from zero with every message;
- She knows **where she is, what time it is, the weather, and what day it is**;
- She **does not write her own lines**: the plugin only supplies the background, and how she speaks is up to the large model.

---

## Features



### Body and routine

- **Body state**: energy, drowsiness, sleep debt, hunger, discomfort, alertness, and willingness to talk (social drive) change with rest and activity; different values mean different states;
- **Social energy**: chatting consumes it and being alone restores it; when tired, she looks after herself first (can be turned off);
- **Sleep**: if she doesn't get enough, she won't wake up properly. Messages don't reschedule her while she sleeps, but the disturbance is recorded as “being disturbed”;
- **Menstrual cycle**: 8 phases, each with its own physical feel, and they also affect some state changes;
- **Dreams**: she dreams while asleep, and for a short time after waking she hasn't fully recovered.

### Schedule

- **Dynamic schedule**: the day gets interrupted, so it is not the same mechanical routine every day;
- **Schedule interruption**: in private chat, calling her (“are you there”, “keep me company”) makes her put down what she's doing and switch to something else;
- **Resuming suspended tasks**: interrupted activities are suspended for a while, and once free she can return to them on her own;
- **Dedicated material**: a separate set of life material is written for her persona. It is rewritten only when the persona changes, and falls back to the built-in pool if it can't be written;
- **Things she mentioned enter the schedule**: “things to do today” with explicit dates from the conversation are recorded and included in chronological order.
- **Review after scheduling**: before each new schedule segment is loaded, the model reviews whether it “connects” (enough time to get there, possible locations, reasonable durations, no people appearing out of nowhere). If it fails, it is revised according to the stated reasons before use.
- **Immediately continue when free**: when a segment ends, the next one is scheduled right away, without waiting for the throttle interval.

### Emotions and relationships

- **Emotions**: change with interaction; lasting emotions don't reset after a single message;
- **Affection**: relationships deepen, and it can drop after several harsh remarks in a row;
- **Days known**: remembers how long you've known each other, but doesn't force her to bring it up constantly;
- **Relationship stages**: as affection and acquaintance time reach different stages, wording and initiative change accordingly, not just a number;
- **Attention** — …
